/godotengine/godot/issues/117085","id":4005055839,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7uuE1f","user":{"login":"catpocalypse","id":75236551,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjM2NTUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75236551?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/catpocalypse","html_url":"https://github.com/catpocalypse","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catpocalypse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catpocalypse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catpocalypse/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catpocalypse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catpocalypse/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catpocalypse/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catpocalypse/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catpocalypse/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catpocalypse/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-05T13:27:13Z","updated_at":"2026-03-05T13:27:13Z","body":"> To be clear, this did not occur in 4.5 and earlier? Or are you mentioning 4.6.1 because that's the version you use?\n\nThe issue is reproducible in 4.5 as well. I haven’t tested versions earlier than 4.5 yet.\nAlso, I’m seeing different lightmap results between ORMMaterial3D and StandardMaterial3D, even when using the same metallic texture/value.\nWith StandardMaterial3D specifically, when metallic is below 1.0, the contribution from static lights appears in the mesh’s lightmap inversely proportional to the metallic value (lower metallic → stronger baked lighting, higher metallic → weaker baked lighting).","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4005055839/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4113512480","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117085#issuecomment-4113512480","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117085","id":4113512480,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc71Lzgg","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-23T20:29:52Z","updated_at":"2026-03-24T00:37:35Z","body":"I can confirm this on 4.7.dev 64596092a. The issue doesn't occur if you use an ORM map with a fully dielectric (blue channel is `0` throughout, instead of `1` as it is in the MRP). The material's metalness *does* affect lightmap baking, as seen in probes after baking with different ORM maps.\n\nWhen fully smooth, fully metallic materials don't get any ambient diffuse light, only specular light from the environment (or reflection probes if present). Since LightmapGI only bakes diffuse lighting, this needs https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/86135 to be fixed as far as I can tell. https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109737 can also help with this.\n\n**Edit:** I just tested with https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109737 and it completely fixes the issue, as long as **Directional** is enabled in LightmapGI before baking:\n\n<img width=\"2002\" height=\"1238\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/68b9d625-4a77-4ce9-a3b4-f00ac7e1dbbe\" />\n\n___\n\nTherefore, I'll consolidate this in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/63016 as it's due to the same cause.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4113512480/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]